# Rust

## Workspace

- Shared crates are only `crates/core`, `crates/shell`, and `crates/cli`.
- Do not add a crate that duplicates those roles.
- App Rust lives in `programs/<name>/src-tauri/`. Depend on shared crates; do not copy them.
- Root `cargo.toml` is the Cargo workspace. Register members there; do not invent a second workspace file.

## Types and FFI

- Shared FFI / IPC types belong in `crates/core`.
- `crates/shell` is shared shell behavior. `crates/cli` is CLI-only.
- Do not define the same type in a program and a crate.

## Errors

```rust
// BAD — lib / IPC
let v = state.inner.lock().unwrap();

// GOOD
let v = state.inner.lock().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
```

- No `unwrap()` / `expect()` on IPC commands, library paths, or anything that crosses the webview boundary.
